    <string-array name="daily_tips">
        <item>Water in the morning so leaves dry before evening — damp foliage overnight invites fungus.</item>
        <item>Yellow lower leaves often mean overwatering. Check the soil before you reach for the can.</item>
        <item>Rotate houseplants a quarter turn every week for even, upright growth.</item>
        <item>Wipe dusty leaves with a damp cloth — clean leaves photosynthesise better.</item>
        <item>Quarantine new plants for two weeks to stop pests hitching a ride.</item>
        <item>Brown, crispy tips usually point to low humidity or inconsistent watering.</item>
        <item>Sterilise pruning shears between plants to avoid spreading disease.</item>
        <item>Most houseplants need less water in winter when growth slows down.</item>
    </string-array>
